  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reinforcing Integration through Sponsorship Enhancement in Belgium, Italy and Lithuania</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reinforcing integration through sponsorship enhancement in Belgium, Italy and Lithuania - RISEIOM Lithuania, IOM Belgium, and IOM Italy, in close collaboration with national authorities and partners, will commence the execution of the RISE project. This initiative is designed to address the housing needs of beneficiaries of international protection through the development and piloting of community sponsorship programs in Lithuania, Belgium, and Italy.Key objectives include strengthening knowledge and capacity through effective housing solution  assessments, developing customized toolkits for resilient housing solutions, and piloting community sponsorship schemes. The project also aims to foster transnational exchange through six thematic events.The project aspires to encourage more EU Member States to adopt community sponsorship schemes and contribute to a coherent pan-European approach. The project&apos;s findings and experiences will be shared to pave the way for lasting change and innovation in addressing the housing needs of beneficiaries of international protection across Europe.</narrative>
  </description>
